summary:
The case comprises 20 applications against Ukraine (no. 19430/06 and 19 others), lodged with the European Court of Human Rights between 20 April 2006 and 7 September 2010. The applicants are Ukrainian nationals, except the applicant in application no. 64583/09, who is a Russian national. The applications mainly concern the lengthy failure to enforce final domestic decisions given in the applicants’ favour. The domestic judgments entitled the applicants to various pecuniary amounts or to have certain actions taken. They became final and enforceable, but the applicants could not obtain timely enforcement because the authorities failed to take specific budgetary or regulatory measures and because bans were introduced on the attachment and sale of property belonging to State-owned or controlled companies.

The domestic decisions and applicants, as listed, were:
- no. 19430/06, Vasiliy Aleksandrovich Ternovik, Novogrodivka Court, 17 September 1998;
- no. 25358/06, Vasyl Grygorovych Dyabelko, Kovpakivskyy District Court of Sumy, 11 August 2005;
- no. 2555/07, Valeriy Ivanovich Zvenigorodskiy, Leninskyy District Court of Kirovograd, 21 August 2001;
- no. 2560/07, Anatoliy Vasilyevich Pirozhenko and Vladimir Anatolyevich Tomilo, Leninskyy District Court of Kirovograd, 21 August 2001;
- no. 39111/07, Mikhail Viktorovich Kopeyko, Gornyatskyy District Court of Makeyivka, 19 September 2005;
- no. 1777/08, Sergey Aleksandrovich Bobrovskiy, Prymorskyy District Court of Mariupol, 5 July 2004;
- no. 4988/08, Viktoriy Gennadyevich Titarenko, Krasnyy Luch Court, 16 June 2005;
- no. 13791/08, Olga Nikolayevna Skobina, Krasnyy Luch Court, 12 May 2005;
- no. 25997/08, Vladimir Leonidovich Lukichev and Lyudmila Mikhaylovna Belkina, Gagarinskyy District Court of Sevastopol, 26 November 2007;
- no. 27005/08, Nataliya Volodymyrivna Yurchenko, Kozelets Court, 12 November 2007;
- no. 27421/08, Vasyl Mykolayovych Krupa, Kolomyya Court, 11 January 2006;
- no. 27897/08, Igor Fyodorovich Prokopenko, Konotop Court, 6 November 2007;
- no. 42269/08, Vasiliy Petrovich Kochura, Torez Court, 31 January 2002;
- no. 60798/08, Andriy Igorovych Samus, Kyiv City Court of Appeal, 9 June 2003;
- no. 23248/09, Petro Ivanovych Mazharov, Obolonskyy District Court of Kyiv, 13 June 2007;
- no. 64583/09, Vladislav Yevgenyevich Shchegolkov, Gagarinskyy District Court of Sevastopol, 4 April 2007;
- no. 21509/10, Anatoliy Oleksiyovych Gerasko, Higher Administrative Court, 2 April 2008;
- no. 43535/10, Ryurik Petrovich Rodichev, Krasnyy Luch Court, 30 May 2007;
- no. 56208/10, Lyudmila Vladimirovna Shkarina, Krasnyy Luch Court, 15 July 2005;
- no. 20895/09, Mykola Ivanovych Dmytrenko, Prydniprovskyy District Court of Cherkasy, 13 August 2007.

Four decisions were enforced: no. 25358/06 on 2 June 2011; no. 1777/08 on 18 April 2008; no. 20895/09 on 9 July 2009; and no. 64583/09 on 18 January 2011. The domestic decisions in all other applications had not been enforced in full. Some applicants also made submissions concerning factual and legal matters unrelated to the non-enforcement issues. The applications were communicated to the Government on various dates, and the Government later submitted unilateral declarations aimed at resolving the non-enforcement issues.

